{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-8574" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions of the equation $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=-\\frac{1}{4}$ for $-\\pi <x\\le \\pi ,$ what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2},$ rounded to $1$ decimal place?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066983/state.json" "file_sha256" "a2f7bd0492f90795ba6bd5975b67486670831bbc6c6d0ac1781237cfe7fe11d3"} {"question" "q-8574" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-\\frac{1}{4})=-0.252\\,680…≈-0.252\\,7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $-0.252\\,7$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=-0.252\\,7.$\n\nOur first solution lies in the fourth quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}=0.252\\,7.$ Since $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x<0,$ the second solution must lie in the third quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}=0.252\\,7.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066983/assets/8cb3c3ad525f606ec5cc6ef3961577666ab7117b3ce2a17014df989dcb105f57.png)\n\nA second solution $X$ lies in the $3$rd quadrant, and we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =\\pi +{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & =\\pi +0.252\\,7 \\\\  & ≈3.394\\,3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, this value is not in the required domain. To get the second solution ${x}_{2}$ that's within the given domain, we simply subtract $2\\pi :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}=X-2\\pi  & =3.394\\,3-2\\pi ≈-2.888\\,9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=(-0.252\\,7)\\cdot (-2.888\\,9)≈0.7,\n$$\n\nrounded to $1$ decimal place." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066983/state.json" "file_sha256" "a2f7bd0492f90795ba6bd5975b67486670831bbc6c6d0ac1781237cfe7fe11d3"} {"question" "q-8574" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066983/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "32c7c2538cb7e2e4a0a08f06447abdb0186162d54d4e172310c7695b9f243ec5"} {"question" "q-8574" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066983/state.json" "file_sha256" "a2f7bd0492f90795ba6bd5975b67486670831bbc6c6d0ac1781237cfe7fe11d3"} {"question" "q-8574" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0.7"] ["math" "0.8"] ["math" "0.9"] ["math" "1.0"] ["math" "2.3"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066983/state.json" "file_sha256" "a2f7bd0492f90795ba6bd5975b67486670831bbc6c6d0ac1781237cfe7fe11d3"} {"question" "q-8574" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0.7"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066983/state.json" "file_sha256" "a2f7bd0492f90795ba6bd5975b67486670831bbc6c6d0ac1781237cfe7fe11d3"} {"question" "q-319033" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The initial velocity of a particle is $(6i-2j)\\,\\text{km/h}.$ Find the **exact** speed of the particle after $3$ hours if the particle moves with a constant acceleration of $(-i+4j)\\,{\\text{km/h}}^{2}.$\n\n$|v|=$\n\n{{field-1}} $\\text{km/h}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066983/state.json" "file_sha256" "a2f7bd0492f90795ba6bd5975b67486670831bbc6c6d0ac1781237cfe7fe11d3"} {"question" "q-319033" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that when a particle moves with constant acceleration, the velocity vector at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nv=u+at,\n$$\n\nwhere $u$ is the initial velocity, and $a$ is the acceleration of the particle.\n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\nu=6i-2j,\\,a=-i+4j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, after $t=3\\,\\text{h},$ the velocity of the particle will be\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =u+at \\\\  & =(6i-2j)+(-i+4j)(3) \\\\  & =(6i-2j)+(-3i+12j) \\\\  & =(3\\,i+10\\,j)\\,\\text{km/h}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the speed of the particle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|v| & =|3i+10j| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{10}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+100} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{109}\\,\\text{km/h}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066983/state.json" "file_sha256" "a2f7bd0492f90795ba6bd5975b67486670831bbc6c6d0ac1781237cfe7fe11d3"} {"question" "q-319033" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066983/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "32c7c2538cb7e2e4a0a08f06447abdb0186162d54d4e172310c7695b9f243ec5"} {"question" "q-319033" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066983/state.json" "file_sha256" "a2f7bd0492f90795ba6bd5975b67486670831bbc6c6d0ac1781237cfe7fe11d3"} {"question" "q-319033" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{109}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066983/state.json" "file_sha256" "a2f7bd0492f90795ba6bd5975b67486670831bbc6c6d0ac1781237cfe7fe11d3"} {"question" "q-115227" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the inequality $2\\cdot {6}^{x+1}+4<1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066983/state.json" "file_sha256" "a2f7bd0492f90795ba6bd5975b67486670831bbc6c6d0ac1781237cfe7fe11d3"} {"question" "q-115227" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we isolate the exponential term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\cdot {6}^{x+1}+4 & <1 \\\\ 2\\cdot {6}^{x+1} & <-3 \\\\ {6}^{x+1} & <-\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, recall that a positive number raised to any real power is always positive. Since $6>0,$ we have\n\n$$\n{6}^{x+1}>0\n$$\n\nfor every real value of $x.$\n\nTherefore, ${6}^{x+1}$ cannot be less than $-\\frac{3}{2}.$ Hence, the inequality\n\n$$\n{6}^{x+1}<-\\frac{3}{2}\n$$\n\nhas no solutions." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066983/state.json" "file_sha256" "a2f7bd0492f90795ba6bd5975b67486670831bbc6c6d0ac1781237cfe7fe11d3"} {"question" "q-115227" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066983/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "32c7c2538cb7e2e4a0a08f06447abdb0186162d54d4e172310c7695b9f243ec5"} {"question" "q-115227" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066983/state.json" "file_sha256" "a2f7bd0492f90795ba6bd5975b67486670831bbc6c6d0ac1781237cfe7fe11d3"} {"question" "q-115227" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x<-\\frac{3}{2}"] ["math" "x<{log}_{6}⁡3-\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "x>2-{log}_{6}⁡3"] ["text" "all real numbers"] ["text" "no solutions"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066983/state.json" "file_sha256" "a2f7bd0492f90795ba6bd5975b67486670831bbc6c6d0ac1781237cfe7fe11d3"} {"question" "q-115227" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "no solutions"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066983/state.json" "file_sha256" "a2f7bd0492f90795ba6bd5975b67486670831bbc6c6d0ac1781237cfe7fe11d3"} {"question" "q-319550" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine the entry ${a}_{33}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nif its determinant is $-22.$\n\n${a}_{33}^{′}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066983/state.json" "file_sha256" "a2f7bd0492f90795ba6bd5975b67486670831bbc6c6d0ac1781237cfe7fe11d3"} {"question" "q-319550" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since we want the entry ${a}_{33}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{33}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{33} & =(-1)^{3+3}|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\,1\\cdot (2\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot 0)=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{33}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}\\,{c}_{33} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-22}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{11}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066983/state.json" "file_sha256" "a2f7bd0492f90795ba6bd5975b67486670831bbc6c6d0ac1781237cfe7fe11d3"} {"question" "q-319550" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066983/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "32c7c2538cb7e2e4a0a08f06447abdb0186162d54d4e172310c7695b9f243ec5"} {"question" "q-319550" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066983/state.json" "file_sha256" "a2f7bd0492f90795ba6bd5975b67486670831bbc6c6d0ac1781237cfe7fe11d3"} {"question" "q-319550" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{1}{11}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066983/state.json" "file_sha256" "a2f7bd0492f90795ba6bd5975b67486670831bbc6c6d0ac1781237cfe7fe11d3"} {"question" "q-71775" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If ${f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{9}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}},$ then $f(x)=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066983/state.json" "file_sha256" "a2f7bd0492f90795ba6bd5975b67486670831bbc6c6d0ac1781237cfe7fe11d3"} {"question" "q-71775" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{arcsec}\\,x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x)=\\int {f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{9}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{9}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =9\\int \\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =9\\text{ arcsec }x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066983/state.json" "file_sha256" "a2f7bd0492f90795ba6bd5975b67486670831bbc6c6d0ac1781237cfe7fe11d3"} {"question" "q-71775" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066983/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "32c7c2538cb7e2e4a0a08f06447abdb0186162d54d4e172310c7695b9f243ec5"} {"question" "q-71775" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066983/state.json" "file_sha256" "a2f7bd0492f90795ba6bd5975b67486670831bbc6c6d0ac1781237cfe7fe11d3"} {"question" "q-71775" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3\\text{ arcsec }x+C"] ["math" "3\\text{ arctan }x+C"] ["math" "9\\text{ arcsec }x+C"] ["math" "9\\text{ arcsin }x+C"] ["math" "9\\text{ arctan }x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066983/state.json" "file_sha256" "a2f7bd0492f90795ba6bd5975b67486670831bbc6c6d0ac1781237cfe7fe11d3"} {"question" "q-71775" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "9\\text{ arcsec }x+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066983/state.json" "file_sha256" "a2f7bd0492f90795ba6bd5975b67486670831bbc6c6d0ac1781237cfe7fe11d3"} {"question" "q-113624" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The coefficient of ${z}^{9}{x}^{3}$ in the expansion of ${(z+4x)}^{12}$ is" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066983/state.json" "file_sha256" "a2f7bd0492f90795ba6bd5975b67486670831bbc6c6d0ac1781237cfe7fe11d3"} {"question" "q-113624" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The binomial theorem states that for any positive integer $n,$ we have\n \n\n$$\n(a+b)^{n}=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{0}){a}^{n}{b}^{0}+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{1}){a}^{n-1}{b}^{1}+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{2}){a}^{n-2}{b}^{2}+…+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{n}){a}^{0}{b}^{n}.\n$$\n\nIn the case of ${(z+4x)}^{12},$ we have $a=z,$ $b=4x,$ and $n=12.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(z+4x)}^{12}=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{12}{0}){z}^{12}(4x)^{0}+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{12}{1}){z}^{12-1}(4x)^{1}+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{12}{2}){z}^{12-2}(4x)^{2}+⋯+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{12}{12}){z}^{12-12}(4x)^{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom here, we see that the ${z}^{9}{x}^{3}$ term must be\n\n$$\n(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{12}{3}){z}^{12-3}(4x)^{3}.\n$$\n\nSimplifying this term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{12}{3}){z}^{12-3}(4x)^{3} & =220{z}^{9}\\cdot {4}^{3}{x}^{3} \\\\  & =220{z}^{9}\\cdot 64{x}^{3} \\\\  & =14\\,080{z}^{9}{x}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coefficient of ${z}^{9}{x}^{3}$ is $14\\,080.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066983/state.json" "file_sha256" "a2f7bd0492f90795ba6bd5975b67486670831bbc6c6d0ac1781237cfe7fe11d3"} {"question" "q-113624" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066983/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "32c7c2538cb7e2e4a0a08f06447abdb0186162d54d4e172310c7695b9f243ec5"} {"question" "q-113624" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066983/state.json" "file_sha256" "a2f7bd0492f90795ba6bd5975b67486670831bbc6c6d0ac1781237cfe7fe11d3"} {"question" "q-113624" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "14\\,080"] ["math" "1\\,320"] ["math" "220"] ["math" "3\\,520"] ["math" "880"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066983/state.json" "file_sha256" "a2f7bd0492f90795ba6bd5975b67486670831bbc6c6d0ac1781237cfe7fe11d3"} {"question" "q-113624" 